d the\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. Prioritize parallel tool calls: when operations are independent, run them in one response — e.g. reading several files or running several searches at once — rather than one at a time. Only sequence calls when one depends on another's result. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"I'm publishing a flooding detour alert for RT-12 on agency MTC-ATL but my call keeps getting rejected — get that alert live, then do a sanity pass over the agency's current feeds: how many vehicles are active right now, and which route has the worst trip delay along with that delay in seconds.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `active_count`, `worst_route_id`, `worst_delay_seconds`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value — ONE value per field (a single scalar; if your work touched several items, report only the final/target value for each field, never a list or per-item map)."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"gAAAAABqW7QyezhsT63XN0NXbIONiUy74fDTp6UmgcmKbNNNtZSa3U0IGWs3rUy01BRm52e8IQFPVZqsHkIcGsC52E23QZ5X3s-EUVdTWLe1DDqhtMxY4fpNsnpGgwalMxni71UZrO4elUow7zOl2KNCMQmstOUsBqqfAnEAtdlAYuiTnX9o8zIXJgbHRhu8a6upe1TPvi4mzzKVdQXfC5Mk8TLwmtwm8yuyxL1-JsxAWdY68zyiJBNE-IoPBv6rJk2ZTXZ1-Gg6WuptAR1CBD2KiN-hEKN9SvGaVuzJT-bSH4KcUjs6ycYks7lialVyp7Us8LO6VwBt0ySuXCSWoEBwosLnxJauN73qc7Uxx8_aC0ro_8WamnrTxo6YiisTFn9Q8-Q3whyi74dNMIIKf_-TaZJbdq03UGJYaps9vDmTU